# Veripsa release gate (auto-discovered). One gate per file -> two PRs adding gates add two
# FILES, never a shared line -> no false merge conflict on registration. register_gate is
# defined in run_gates.sh. Format: register_gate <test> <marker> <name> <ok_blurb> <desc> [tail]
register_gate "tests/test_tamper_account_authority.py" "TAMPER ACCOUNT-AUTHORITY GATE: PASS" "tamper account-authority" "tamper account-authority (the webhook->tenant binding cannot be forged: F1 set_account_plan_with_authority re-pins from the connection -> a marketplace payload account.id that MISMATCHES the connection-routed tenant is REFUSED [no force-downgrade DoS], while an own-tenant purchase AND a no-installation FIRST purchase both SUCCEED [pre-install purchase allowed -- GitHub's HMAC is the authority]; F2 the per-event processor makes the owner<->installation check STRUCTURAL -> an event whose repository.owner.id disagrees with the delivering installation.account.id is DROPPED fail-soft [clean no-op, content-free log, never a 500, no tenant pin], while the consistent common case proceeds and its claim lands)" "tamper-resistance: the account-resolution authority of the webhook->tenant binding cannot be forced by a payload (SECURITY-critical: F1 payload-account ownership check + F2 owner<->installation structural assertion)" 22
